<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n24193" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δέσποινα</span></b> , ἡ, fem. of
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δεσπότης,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>mistress, lady of the
			house,</i> of Penelope, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				14.127
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄλοχος δ.,</span> of the wife of
				<i><span class="en">Nestor, 3.403</span></i>;
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γυνὴ δ.,</span> of Arete, <i><span class="en">
				7.347
			</span></i>; <i>mistress</i> of a slave, <i><span class="en">
				<u>POxy.</u>
				49.4
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(i/ii A. D.)</span>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>BGU</u>
				55 ii 5
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(ii A. D.)</span>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>princess, queen,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. Κόλχων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>P.</u>
					4.11
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κύπρου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					122.14
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δέσποιν᾽ ἁπασῶν, πότνι᾽ Ἀθηναίων
					πόλι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Com.Adesp.</u>
					340.1
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> coupled with
			the names of goddesses, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. Ἑκάτη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					388
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἄρτεμις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>El.</u>
					626
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				B.
				10.117
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. νύμφη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					342
				</span></i>
			; esp. as a name of Persephone, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Lg.</u>
				796b
			</span></i>; in Arcadia, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				5(2).514
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Lycosura</span>), <i><span class="en">
				Paus.
				8.37.1
			</span></i>-<i><span class="en">
				10
			</span></i>; of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κύπρις,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Xenarch.
				4.21
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b> in Thessaly,
			simply, 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γυνή</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>5.</b> at Rome,
			<u>Empress</u>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>PSI</u>
				1.76.1
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(vi A. D.)</span>, etc.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
